(7189041, 1105671, 15711, '<td valign="top">Love the light.  My eye just keeps going to the cross earring. ;)</td>', 'Love the light.  My eye just keeps going to the cross earring. ;)', '2014-03-12 11:26:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(7189091, 1105621, 30861, '<td valign="top">Lovely piece of work, but it''s not rule of thirds, it''s a "centered composition". That her mouth may fall on the upper ROT horizontal line, and her shoulders as well, on the lower one, doesn''t over-ride the entirely dominant, symmetrical nature of the image.<br/> <br/>Of course, this is neither here nor there in the real world, but I''m afraid in THIS challenge you may be getting dinged for this. Not by me, however.</td>', 'Lovely piece of work, but it''s not rule of thirds, it''s a "centered composition". That her mouth may fall on the upper ROT horizontal line, and her shoulders as well, on the lower one, doesn''t over-ride the entirely dominant, symmetrical nature of the image. Of course, this is neither here nor there in the real world, but I''m afraid in THIS challenge you may be getting dinged for this. Not by me, however.', '2014-03-12 15:10:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(7189093, 1104986, 30861, '<td valign="top">Lovely that the tilt of the child so well matches the tilt of the architecture. I don''t see this as "Deep DOF" myself. I mean, I *know* it''s from "whatever to infinity", but DOF isn''t really being a "technique" here, if you catch my drift? It''s all nit-picking anyway, pay me no heed. Very nice image.</td>', 'Lovely that the tilt of the child so well matches the tilt of the architecture. I don''t see this as "Deep DOF" myself. I mean, I *know* it''s from "whatever to infinity", but DOF isn''t really being a "technique" here, if you catch my drift? It''s all nit-picking anyway, pay me no heed. Very nice image.', '2014-03-12 15:15:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(7189109, 1105543, 163430, '<td valign="top">A bit liberal interpretation of the rule of thirds, but i like it. I like it a lot.</td>', 'A bit liberal interpretation of the rule of thirds, but i like it. I like it a lot.', '2014-03-12 16:46:17.000000', NULL, 1),
